/-- ★★ THE BREAKING DIRECTION MOVES THE IDENTITY (N295 `Lmul_one` + `Lmul_moves_one_ne`): the arena's
    own Jordan left-multiplication `L₀ = Lmul (slotA 1)` sends `1 ↦ slotA 1 + slotA 1 ≠ 0`. Unlike a
    derivation (which kills the identity), it MOVES the degenerate spectral point. -/
theorem breaking_direction_moves : Lmul (slotA (1 : O ℚ)) 1 ≠ 0 := Lmul_moves_one_ne

/-- ★★ EVERY SYMMETRY DERIVATION KILLS THE IDENTITY (N295 `derH3_kills_one`): every `T ∈ f₄ = derH3`
    satisfies `T 1 = 0`. So `f₄` FIXES the maximally-degenerate spectral point `diag(1,1,1)` — no
    derivation can split the degeneracy a mass texture needs. -/
theorem symmetry_fixes_identity (T : Module.End ℚ (Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) (O ℚ)))
    (hT : T ∈ derH3) : T 1 = 0 := derH3_kills_one T hT

/-- ★★★ THE DERIVED BREAKING DIRECTION IS OUTSIDE THE SYMMETRY (N295 `Lmul_notMem_derH3`):
    `L₀ = Lmul (slotA 1) ∉ f₄ = derH3`. The direction that lifts the spectral degeneracy is the
